## Conventions

Variables and parameters range over the real numbers. The symbol $\sqrt{u}$ is the nonnegative real square root and requires $u\geq0$. A square root appearing alone in a denominator requires $u>0$. Other denominators must be nonzero. All terminating decimals below are exact rational numbers. Squaring a comparison is used only after establishing that the quantities being squared are nonnegative.

## 924: Evaluate All Ten Expressions

All radicands are nonnegative; every displayed denominator is nonzero.

| Part | Independent derivation | Exact result |
|---|---|---|
| a | $0.3\sqrt{289}=\frac3{10}\cdot17$ | $\frac{51}{10}=5.1$ |
| b | $-4\sqrt{0.81}=-4\cdot\frac9{10}$ | $-\frac{18}{5}=-3.6$ |
| c | $\sqrt{\frac9{49}}-1=\frac37-1$ | $-\frac47$ |
| d | $\frac4{\sqrt{256}}-\frac1{\sqrt{64}}=\frac4{16}-\frac18$ | $\frac18$ |
| e | $2\sqrt{0.0121}+\sqrt{100}=2\cdot\frac{11}{100}+10$ | $\frac{511}{50}=10.22$ |
| f | $\frac{\sqrt{0.16}}{2\sqrt{0.04}}=\frac{2/5}{2(1/5)}$ | $1$ |
| g | $\sqrt{2500}-\sqrt{625}=50-25$ | $25$ |
| h | $\sqrt{\frac{64}{81}}-\frac1{\sqrt9}=\frac89-\frac13$ | $\frac59$ |
